    "title": "Local Veterans Honored at Elmont Memorial Library Ceremony - NewsBreak",
    "text": "17 minutes ago On November 17, 2024, Senator Patricia Canzoneri-Fitzpatrick held a Veterans Hall of Fame Ceremony at the Elmont Memorial Library in Elmont, NY. She recognized 19 local men and women for their service in the United States Armed Forces. Two World War II veterans were among those honored at the event.\nThe ceremony is part of Senator Canzoneri-Fitzpatrick’s work to honor veterans in Senate District 9. She has previously recognized a local veteran each year in Albany through the New York State Senate’s Veterans Hall of Fame.\nSenator Canzoneri-Fitzpatrick, whose family includes veterans, said these ceremonies help show respect for veterans’ service. She has also organized discussions to address veterans’ concerns and support related legislation. Veterans, their families, officials, and community members attended the event. A program listing all honorees was given to attendees.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
